"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[8991],{18991:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"slug":"neft-brent-110-defitsit-zapasy-oktyabr-2026","locale":"en","title":"Oil markets lack 4–6 million barrels a day, with inventories covering part of the gap for now","description":"The world oil market is short of 4–6 million barrels a day. How inventories restrain prices, why they are finite and what expensive oil means for Russia.","blocks":[{"id":"b001","kind":"paragraph","text":"Before the war around Iran, 18–20 million barrels of oil a day passed through the Strait of Hormuz, about 20% of world consumption. Tanker traffic is now disrupted; there were at least 10 incidents involving merchant vessels last week alone. Novak estimates that the market is receiving 4–6 million barrels a day less than needed, with prices reacting and volatility high. He said oil could rise further if the strait situation does not improve."},{"id":"b002","kind":"paragraph","text":"Brent closed on October 16 at $109.86 per barrel, its highest since May, after gaining 4.9% over the week. On the morning of October 19, it fell by 2% to $107.6 after the US postponed tariffs on Russian-oil buyers. DBS analysts expect Brent to remain in a $100–110 range until the US elections on November 3."},{"id":"b003","kind":"paragraph","text":"Imagine a town whose river has run low. Water still comes from taps because the town draws from a reservoir. While its level is high, only the news reminds residents about the drought. As it falls, each new rainless day becomes more alarming and water prices rise faster. Oil inventories work similarly. They fell by about 507 million barrels from February to August, an average of 2.8 million a day. Lower consumption covers the rest of the gap: above $100, buyers economize."},{"id":"b004","kind":"paragraph","text":"Governments have also tapped reserves. In March, International Energy Agency countries agreed to release 400 million barrels, the largest such action in history. Releases are gradual; in October, G7 countries decided to accelerate them with 100 million barrels over 4 months. Agency members\' government stocks fell from more than 1.2 billion barrels in March to about 1.1 billion. Saudi Aramco\'s chief estimated replenishment could take up to 2 years, and only after the strait reopens."},{"id":"b005","kind":"paragraph","text":"For Russia, expensive oil cuts both ways. Urals averaged $92.08 per barrel in September, 1.37 times August\'s price. The budget receives taxes based on that price only in October because oil companies pay for the previous month. September oil and gas revenue meanwhile fell by 22% year-on-year to 452.4 billion rubles. The fuel compensation mechanism had the greatest effect: more than 300 billion rubles went to oil companies for selling gasoline and diesel domestically below overseas prices. The higher world oil prices rise, the larger that compensation becomes."},{"id":"b006","kind":"paragraph","text":"Iran proposed a 7-point plan to the US for reopening the strait, with conditions including removal of the American blockade of Iranian ports and sanctions on Iranian oil. An agreement would reopen the strait and stop inventories shrinking, removing part of the price premium. Delay would thin the cushion, making every new tanker incident move prices more strongly. Even in the best case, replenishing stocks will support oil demand long after reopening."},{"id":"b007","kind":"heading","text":"How much oil is the world market missing?"},{"id":"b008","kind":"paragraph","text":"Deputy Prime Minister Alexander Novak estimated the shortfall at 4–6 million barrels a day. Before the war, 18–20 million barrels a day passed through the Strait of Hormuz, about 20% of world consumption."},{"id":"b009","kind":"heading","text":"Why is oil not rising even faster despite this deficit?"},{"id":"b010","kind":"paragraph","text":"Inventories cover part of the gap. Global stocks fell by about 507 million barrels from February to August, while IEA countries release government reserves. Lower consumption at high prices covers the remainder."},{"id":"b011","kind":"heading","text":"Does Russia\'s budget immediately earn more from expensive oil?"},{"id":"b012","kind":"paragraph","text":"Not immediately and not in full. Taxes based on September\'s Urals price of $92.08 reach the budget in October. In September, oil and gas revenue fell by 22% year-on-year to 452.4 billion rubles. More than 300 billion rubles funded compensation to oil companies for containing domestic fuel prices."}],"sources":[{"label":"Russia sees a possible oil-price rise under one condition","url":"https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/18/v-rossii-dopustili-rost-tsen-na-neft-pri-odnom-uslovii"},{"label":"Oil slips from 5-month high as Trump\'s Russia sanctions waiver may bring more supplies","url":"https://www.brecorder.com/news/40444883/oil-slips-from-5-month-high-as-trumps-russia-sanctions-waiver-may-bring-more-supplies"},{"label":"Brent Crude Oil Price Today — Russia Sanctions Waiver Pulls Oil to $108","url":"https://financefeeds.com/brent-crude-oil-price-108-trump-russia-sanctions-waiver-diesel-bull-113-bear-103/"},{"label":"Emergency Oil Releases Risk Draining the World\'s Last Supply Cushion","url":"https://oilprice.com/Energy/Crude-Oil/Emergency-Oil-Releases-Risk-Draining-the-Worlds-Last-Supply-Cushion.html"},{"label":"The IEA wants to empty its oil reserves faster","url":"https://fortune.com/2026/10/12/global-emergency-oil-stocks-iea-strategic-petroleum-reserve-gao/"},{"label":"Russian oil becomes almost one-and-a-half times more expensive","url":"https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/05/urals/"},{"label":"Hormuz Is Turning Shipping\'s Fuel Bill Into a Supply Crisis","url":"https://oilprice.com/Geopolitics/Middle-East/Hormuz-Is-Turning-Shippings-Fuel-Bill-Into-a-Supply-Crisis.html"}],"sourceBodySha256":"a6721b5d10f7db363b29126d03c2d3cf16674ee17781634fc68dc894cb116856"}')}}]);